    {
      "case": "Brent chronology and rejected February–October link",
      "source_ids": [
        "DCP-LETT-2048F",
        "DCP-LETT-2158",
        "DCP-LETT-2850"
      ],
      "requirement": "Keep 2048F as Darwin’s 7 February 1857 response to a missing earlier Brent letter and 2158 as an incomplete 23 October 1857 incoming fragment. The phrase identifying a letter received the morning after yesterday points to a missing 22 October query, not 2048F; do not create a February–October pair. Preserve open or supplied dates and the fragment boundary. No receipt date for Darwin is established. Separately, 2850 is after August 1856 with an unresolved period/date; its XML August 2 lower and 1882 upper are not exact composition evidence. Preserve its fragment and uncertain source wording; do not silently turn the index envelope into a retrieval date.",
      "exact_source_evidence": [
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-2048F",
          "body_paragraph": 4,
          "quote": "I was writing to Mr. Tegetmeier this morning, & had asked him to apply to Carstang for one; but I have struck out the passage.",
          "char_start": 94,
          "char_end": 220,
          "source_sha256": "561704905c731aa440386d9044df758963a6025e1119a27435a5194be1d229fe",
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div/div[1]/div[2]/p[5]"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-2158",
          "body_paragraph": 1,
          "quote": "Yours of yesterday came to hand this morning",
          "char_start": 0,
          "char_end": 44,
          "source_sha256": "f471c970242a62bee31d6e5233116df98d4d9b5ca9abbcfbd0c13bf1bf517777",
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[2]/p[2]"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-2850",
